{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":39470,"items":[{"institution":[{"name":"R\u012bga Stradi\u0146\u0161 University"}],"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,5,14]],"date-time":"2025-05-14T08:22:08Z","timestamp":1747210928691,"version":"3.40.5"},"reference-count":1,"publisher":"Riga Stradins University","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"DOI":"10.25143\/prom-rsu_2012-02_dts","type":"dissertation","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,9,4]],"date-time":"2023-09-04T14:16:57Z","timestamp":1693837017000},"approved":{"date-parts":[[2012,3,14]]},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["The Role of Core Biopsy in Kidney Graft Pathology Diagnostics. Summary of the Doctoral Thesis"],"prefix":"10.25143","author":[{"sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4011-3590","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Suhorukovs","family":"Vadims","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"R\u012bga Stradi\u0146\u0161 University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"10768","reference":[{"key":"ref1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","unstructured":"BioSharing: Harnessing Metadata Standards For The\n          Data Commons. Susanna-Assunta Sansone, Alejandra Gonzalez-Beltran,\n          Philippe Rocca-Serra, PeterMcQuilton, Massimiliano Izzo, Allyson Lister,\n          Milo Thurston. bioRxiv 144147","DOI":"10.25143\/prom-rsu_2012-02_dts"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,9,4]],"date-time":"2023-09-04T14:20:54Z","timestamp":1693837254000},"score":30.224735,"degree":["Dr. med."],"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/dspace.rsu.lv\/jspui\/handle\/123456789\/14402"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[null]]},"references-count":1,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.25143\/prom-rsu_2012-02_dts"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,13]],"date-time":"2023-10-13T11:14:55Z","timestamp":1697195695311},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Vilnius University Press","issue":"30","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2014,4,25]],"date-time":"2014-04-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1398384000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["RePhi"],"abstract":"<jats:p>My article investigates the situation, goals, and discourse praxis of professors supervising\u00a0doctoral students writing in English. It is part of a wider project examining student-teacher\u00a0interaction which is designed to improve written communication, particularly at the higher\u00a0levels of academic study. Like the students they supervise, the five professors studied are\u00a0English as a Foreign Language users, and all give instruction exclusively in English. Based\u00a0on separate interviews with each professor, my study demonstrates that there is a tendency\u00a0among doctoral supervisors to focus on the content and form of the thesis to the detriment of\u00a0socio-cultural practice, i.e., the discourse between the professor and student, as well as the\u00a0recognition of the text as a piece of social practice, shaped by a particular kind of academic\u00a0public and the rules of scholarship that have been developed over time. The type of social\u00a0practice that students bring with them varies from culture to culture. I argue that a doctoral\u00a0thesis bears witness not only to the student\u2019s ability to conduct research at a high level, but\u00a0also to the creation of a distinct scholarly identity that is the result of effective discourse\u00a0between professor and student, whereby the professor communicates \u201cthe rules of the game\u201d\u00a0that lead to a successful career both at university and after. My paper reflects on how we as\u00a0teachers\/supervisors can promote the formation of scholarly identity through the medium of\u00a0English as a Foreign Language. I do so by focusing on the five supervisors\u2019 knowledge of\u00a0English, their ability to provide guidance in English, and their awareness of the importance\u00a0of promoting scholarly identity in English. The article concludes with some reflections on the\u00a0type of support required, if any, from native English teachers.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.15388\/respectus.2014.25.30.8","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2019,8,12]],"date-time":"2019-08-12T12:14:33Z","timestamp":1565612073000},"page":"105-117","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Supervising in English: The Doctoral Thesis, Professor\/Student Discourse, and Social Practice"],"prefix":"10.15388","volume":"25","author":[{"given":"Jane","family":"Mattisson","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"6097","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2014,4,25]]},"container-title":["Respectus Philologicus"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.zurnalai.vu.lt\/respectus-philologicus\/article\/download\/13780\/12691","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/www.zurnalai.vu.lt\/respectus-philologicus\/article\/download\/13780\/12691","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,12]],"date-time":"2023-10-12T05:27:12Z","timestamp":1697088432000},"score":30.135887,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.zurnalai.vu.lt\/respectus-philologicus\/article\/view\/13780"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2014,4,25]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"30","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2014,4,25]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.15388\/respectus.2014.25.30.8","ISSN":["2335-2388","1392-8295"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2335-2388","type":"electronic"},{"value":"1392-8295","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2014,4,25]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,5]],